        "original_id": "eeb2b510-4da2-564f-9dd8-a006c218a3da",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Washington, D.C.\n- Organizations: St. Elizabeths Hospital, Providence Hospital, American Psychiatric Association\n- People: Winfred Overholser\n- Topics: psychiatric hospitals, hospital history\n\nFacts:\n- St. Elizabeths Hospital opened in 1855 as the first federally operated psychiatric hospital in the United States.\n- Providence Hospital in Washington, D.C., was founded in 1861 and is the longest continuously operating hospital in the District.\n- Winfred Overholser was born in 1892.\n- Winfred Overholser was an American psychiatrist and served as president of the American Psychiatric Association.\n- Winfred Overholser served for 25 years as superintendent of St. Elizabeths Hospital in Washington, D.C.\n- Winfred Overholser died on October 6, 1964.",
